''Ready to achieve ultimate glory in combat? Then keep reading...''

[[File:Combat Achievements Expansion- Rewards (1).png|center|600px]]


Since we released Combat Achievements a year or so ago (how time flies!) we've added loads of new content to the game – with this ever-increasing task list, we want to ensure that you're also getting plenty of new rewards.

One of the biggest complaints about Combat Achievements is that they're not rewarding, especially considering the amount of time it takes to complete higher tiers. When we look at the data, we can see that even players with the combat skill to beat the tiers are rarely doing so – and this tells us that you need greater incentives to get those 'cheeves.

We've also talked about a potential, long-term solution on livestream before, but here's the lowdown for those of you who missed it: we want to explore a points-based system for Combat Achievements, similar to the mechanics used to unlock Leagues rewards.

We'd give every Combat Achievement its own point value, with harder tasks awarding more points. This would let you pick and choose which tasks to try, while still reaping awesome benefits. Some of you might choose to complete all the Easy tasks, while more experienced players could complete one Hard and two Medium tasks and get the same reward.

We believe this is a more player-friendly approach and it's something you've been asking us to investigate for some time, so let us know if you would be interested in us continuing our exploration.

In the meantime, let's talk rewards!

==Changes to Current Rewards==
[[File:Combat Achievements Expansion- Rewards (2).png|center|600px]]


Before we take a look at the new rewards on offer, we'd like to make a couple of tweaks to the current selection, to make them a little more motivating.

First up, we have the ''''Like A Boss' Bonus''' – we'd like to buff your reward based on your Kill Count when assigned a boss task:
* Easy: Up to 40 Boss Kills (3 more than the current reward)
* Medium: Up to 45 Boss Kills (6 more than the current reward)
* Hard: Up to 50 Boss Kills (9 more than the current reward)
* Elite: Up to 55 Boss Kills (12 more than the current reward)
* Master: Up to 60 Boss Kills (14 more than the current reward)
* Grandmaster: Up to 65 Boss Kills (15 more than the current reward)

Speaking of Kill Counts, we want to reduce the requirements for the '''God Wars Dungeon KC Entry''':
* Hard: 35 Follower Kill Count (a 3 kill improvement from the current reward)
* Elite: 30 Follower Kill Count (a 6 kill improvement from the current reward)
* Master: 25 Follower Kill Count (an 8 kill improvement from the current reward)
* Grandmaster: 15 Follower Kill Count (a 15 kill improvement from the current reward)

{{News Poll|1|Should we improve the 'Like A Boss' bonuses and God Wars Kill Count Reduction rewards currently offered from Combat Achievements?}}

